      <p>DriverBench is a lightweight analysis and reporting tool for builders and repair benches already collecting loudspeaker impedance data.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Import CSV and ZMA-style impedance data</li>
        <li>Generate magnitude and phase reports</li>
        <li>Compare a driver against a golden reference</li>
        <li>Match two drivers and flag tolerance excursions</li>
        <li>Attach job ID, asset, operator, and notes</li>
        <li>Export normalized CSV and JSON</li>
        <li>Python 3.10+ with no third-party packages required</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> DriverBench does not measure a speaker by itself. It analyzes data from an existing measurement setup. A PASS result only means the compared curves stayed inside the tolerances you selected.</p>
